{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets.md; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md; sed -n '1,130p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/capability_catalog.go; sed -n '790,855p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/capability_catalog.go; rg -n 'func applyReviewAnswer|func reviewAnswerApplied' pose-mcp/internal/cli/configuration_review.go; rg -n 'func PlanAdoptionEffects|func ApplyAdoption' pose-mcp/internal/pose\"","aggregated_output":"---\nslug: pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-14\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority:            # integer >= 0 (lower = higher priority); ordering preference, not a blocker\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface:             # optional: minimal | standard | full (default) — minimal drops Tasks and derivable report sections; `pose specs facts <slug>` derives them\ndelivers: capability:adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nFazer a prévia de `pose adopt --request <act-id>` mostrar as mudanças de policy que o `--apply` grava, e o manual distribuído descrever o perfil de revisão do pose-dist como do pose-dist.\n\n### Business value\nEm 2026-11-14 o mantenedor do harne8 respondeu a revisão de configuração 7.4.1: adotar `closeout-review-policy` com `when-justified`. A prévia de `pose adopt --request` mostrou só `adopt.apply=false`, sem nenhuma mudança, mas o `--apply` gravaria `milestone_review_required=never` e `roadmap_review_required=never`, os padrões do catálogo: a instância teria valores que ninguém escolheu, sem aviso. A adoção foi feita pelo caminho direto, que mostra os valores. No mesmo `pose update`, o manual instalado no harne8 passou a dizer \"o perfil de revisão Claude deste repositório\", texto que descreve o perfil do próprio pose-dist.\n\n### Constraints\n- O caminho por solicitação continua recusando o par de valores (decisão da spec `pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit`, teste `TestCloseoutReviewPolicyAdoptRequestRefusesThePair`).\n\n### Non-goals\n- Não mudar o que uma resposta aplica.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: The preview of an answered adoption request shall name every policy change its apply writes, the catalog adoption included, as the direct adoption path does.\n- R2: For closeout-review-policy, the preview shall say that the request adopts the catalog default and name the command that chooses other values.\n- R3: The distributed manual shall describe the sandboxed Claude review profile as the one pose-dist qualified for its own reviews, not as the installing repository's.\n\n### Non-functional\n- Nenhum.\n\n### Security\n- Nenhuma mudança.\n\n### Compatibility\n- Nenhum formato muda.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n- `cli/adopt.go`: a prévia de uma solicitação respondida aplica a adoção do catálogo a uma cópia em memória da policy e lista as mudanças.\n- Manual: uma frase nas quatro cópias.\n\n### Artifacts\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/adopt.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/configuration_review_test.go\n- modified: POSE.md\n- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\nComposto por `pose adopt --request` e `pose setup`. Check permanente `adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/cli -run 'TestAnAnsweredAdoptionPreviewNamesThePolicyItWrites|TestConfigurationReview|TestCloseoutReviewPolicyAdoptRequestRefusesThePair' -count=1`.\n\n### API/contract changes\n- A prévia ganha linhas `adopt.change` e, para a política de fechamento, `adopt.values`.\n\n### Data/storage changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Technical risks\n- Nenhum.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Prévia com as mudanças do catálogo (R1, R2).\n- [x] Frase do manual (R3).\n\n### Validation\n- [x] Teste da prévia contra o apply.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nTeste de CLI: uma solicitação de adoção respondida mostra na prévia cada mudança que a adoção do catálogo grava, e o apply adota a capacidade.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -count=1`\n- Scope: pose-mcp\n- Expected: verde\n\n### Execution log\n- Date: 2026-11-14\n- Environment: Linux, Go 1.26.\n- Notes: o teste novo reprova sem a mudança em `adopt.go` (a prévia não nomeia a mudança) e passa com ela.\n\n### Results summary\n- Successes: prévia e apply coincidem.\n- Failures: nenhuma.\n- Warnings: nenhum.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestAnAnsweredAdoptionPreviewNamesThePolicyItWrites check:adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\n- R2 [satisfied] check:adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestConfigurationReviewAsksOncePerCapabilityAndChangesNothing\n\n### Known gaps\n- O fixture de instância revisada desta versão não pergunta a política de fechamento; a linha `adopt.values` é coberta pela leitura do código, não por teste.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nA prévia de uma solicitação de adoção respondida lista as mudanças que o apply grava e, para a política de fechamento, diz que o padrão do catálogo é adotado e como escolher outros valores; o manual distribuído atribui o perfil de revisão sandboxed ao pose-dist.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n- `cli/adopt.go`, teste, quatro cópias do manual, matriz.\n\n### Validation executed\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver ./internal/scaffold -count=1`\n- Result: verde.\n\n### Residual risks\n- Nenhum.\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n- [open] F1: deixar a revisão de configuração perguntar os valores de uma capacidade parametrizada (a política de fechamento) nas próprias opções da solicitação, para que a resposta do mantenedor decida também os valores. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-13)\n# Rule: Backend Go\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for HTTP handlers, domain services, persistence, concurrency, and integrations between Go services.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Handle and propagate errors with enough context for diagnosis.\n- Validate handler input and return HTTP status codes consistent with the contract.\n- Keep business rules in service or domain layers, not in transport code.\n- Honor `context.Context` for timeouts and cancellation.\n- Put data access behind clear interfaces that support testing.\n- Use structured logs without exposing sensitive data.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Ignoring error returns, including `_` for critical errors.\n- Using `panic` in ordinary request flows instead of controlled error handling.\n- Coupling handlers directly to concrete repository implementations without an abstraction.\n- Running unbounded or unpaginated queries in potentially large endpoints.\n- Introducing concurrency without adequate synchronization or race protection.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `go test ./...` in the affected scope.\n- Run `go test -race ./...` when concurrency changes.\n- Run `go vet ./...` without blocking findings.\n- Run the applicable Go lint check, such as `golangci-lint`, without critical errors.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\npackage pose\n\n// The capability catalog describes everything a project can adopt — what it\n// changes day to day, since which version, whether a new instance gets it,\n// what it requires — and how to turn it on and off (spec\n// pose-capability-catalog). `pose adopt`, `pose setup`, install and the update\n// review all read it, so a capability is described once and toggled the same\n// way everywhere. A decision not to adopt is recorded too, in\n// .pose/policy/adoption-decisions.json, so nothing decided is asked again.\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\n// PolicyDocs are the raw policy documents a capability writes. Raw maps keep\n// every key the engine does not model; the reader validates them on Write.\ntype PolicyDocs struct {\n\tReview map[string]any\n\tDoR    map[string]any\n\t// Root is the instance the documents were loaded from, for an adoption\n\t// that copies a declared value (the project id) into policy.\n\tRoot string\n\n\treviewOriginal, dorOriginal []byte\n\t// reviewRead and dorRead are the bytes each document was loaded from:\n\t// Write publishes only over them (spec\n\t// pose-writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication R2).\n\treviewRead, dorRead PublishExpectation\n\t// FS is the filesystem the documents were loaded from; a prerequisite\n\t// that checks an installed file reads it there.\n\tFS Files\n}\n\nfunc LoadPolicyDocsIn(files Files, root string) (PolicyDocs, error) {\n\tdocs := PolicyDocs{Root: root, FS: files}\n\treads := map[string]PublishExpectation{}\n\tload := func(rel string) (map[string]any, []byte, error) {\n\t\traw, err := files.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"policy\", rel))\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\t\treads[rel] = PublishExpectation{Mode: ExpectAbsent}\n\t\t\treturn map[string]any{}, nil, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treads[rel] = ExpectBytes(raw, true)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tdoc := map[string]any{}\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &doc); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: invalid .pose/policy/%s: %w\", rel, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tcanonical, _ := json.Marshal(doc)\n\t\treturn doc, canonical, nil\n\t}\n\tvar err error\n\tif docs.Review, docs.reviewOriginal, err = load(\"review.json\"); err != nil {\n\t\treturn docs, err\n\t}\n\tif docs.DoR, docs.dorOriginal, err = load(\"dor.json\"); err != nil {\n\t\treturn docs, err\n\t}\n\tdocs.reviewRead, docs.dorRead = reads[\"review.json\"], reads[\"dor.json\"]\n\treturn docs, nil\n}\n\n// LoadPolicyDocs reads and writes the filesystem directly; LoadPolicyDocsIn takes the\n// operation's files.\nfunc LoadPolicyDocs(root string) (PolicyDocs, error) {\n\treturn LoadPolicyDocsIn(NativeFiles(), root)\n}\n\n// Rendered returns the documents as they would be written, validated by the\n// readers, and which of them changed.\nfunc (d PolicyDocs) Rendered(store Store) (review, dor []byte, reviewChanged, dorChanged bool, err error) {\n\treviewCanonical, _ := json.Marshal(d.Review)\n\tdorCanonical, _ := json.Marshal(d.DoR)\n\treviewChanged = !bytes.Equal(reviewCanonical, d.reviewOriginal)\n\tdorChanged = !bytes.Equal(dorCanonical, d.dorOriginal)\n\tif review, err = json.MarshalIndent(d.Review, \"\", \"  \"); err != nil {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\treview = append(review, '\\n')\n\tif dor, err = json.MarshalIndent(d.DoR, \"\", \"  \"); err != nil {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tdor = append(dor, '\\n')\n\tif reviewChanged {\n\t\tif _, err = store.ParseReviewPolicyDocument(review); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif dorChanged {\n\t\tvar policy DoRPolicy\n\t\tif err = json.Unmarshal(dor, &policy); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\tif policy.AdoptedAt != \"\" {\n\t\t\tif _, perr := time.Parse(\"2006-01-02\", policy.AdoptedAt); perr != nil {\n\t\t\t\terr = fmt.Errorf(\"pose: dor.json adopted_at must be YYYY-MM-DD, got %q\", policy.AdoptedAt)\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn\n}\n\n// Write persists the changed documents after the readers accept them.\nfunc (d PolicyDocs) Write(root string, store Store) error {\n\trequestedRoot, err := canonicalGovernanceRoot(root)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tstoreRoot, err := canonicalGovernanceRoot(store.Root)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif governanceRootKey(requestedRoot) != governanceRootKey(storeRoot) {\n\t\treturn governanceGuardError(ErrGovernanceWriteGuardRootBinding, \"policy.docs.write\", requestedRoot, fmt.Errorf(\"policy path root %s does not match Store root %s\", requestedRoot, storeRoot))\n\t}\n\tstore.Root = requestedRoot\n\treturn store.withGovernanceWriteGuard(\"policy.docs.write\", func(guarded Store) error {\n\t\treturn d.write(guarded.Root, guarded)\n\t})\n\n// closeoutPairPresent reports a policy that carries the closeout review pair,\n// whose schema (5) no other capability may lower.\nfunc closeoutPairPresent(docs PolicyDocs) bool {\n\t_, milestone := docs.Review[MilestoneReviewRequiredKey]\n\t_, roadmap := docs.Review[RoadmapReviewRequiredKey]\n\treturn milestone || roadmap\n}\n\n// SetCloseoutReviewPolicy writes both closeout review keys and schema 5\n// together (spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit R2, R6). It is the\n// one producer for adoption, install defaults and later changes, so the pair\n// is never written half.\nfunc SetCloseoutReviewPolicy(docs PolicyDocs, milestone, roadmap string) ([]string, error) {\n\tif !validCloseoutReviewValue(milestone) || !validCloseoutReviewValue(roadmap) {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: %s and %s take never, when-justified or always (got %q, %q)\", MilestoneReviewRequiredKey, RoadmapReviewRequiredKey, milestone, roadmap)\n\t}\n\tchanges := []string{}\n\tif schemaVersionOf(docs) != CloseoutReviewPolicySchemaVersion {\n\t\tdocs.Review[\"schema_version\"] = CloseoutReviewPolicySchemaVersion\n\t\tchanges = append(changes, fmt.Sprintf(\"set schema_version=%d\", CloseoutReviewPolicySchemaVersion))\n\t}\n\tfor _, pair := range [][2]string{{MilestoneReviewRequiredKey, milestone}, {RoadmapReviewRequiredKey, roadmap}} {\n\t\tif current, _ := docs.Review[pair[0]].(string); current != pair[1] {\n\t\t\tdocs.Review[pair[0]] = pair[1]\n\t\t\tchanges = append(changes, \"set \"+pair[0]+\"=\"+pair[1])\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn changes, nil\n}\n\n// CloseoutReviewPolicyEffective describes the rule a policy applies today: the\n// adopted pair, or the legacy rule it keeps until adoption.\nfunc CloseoutReviewPolicyEffective(docs PolicyDocs) (adopted bool, milestone, roadmap string) {\n\tif !closeoutPairPresent(docs) {\n\t\treturn false, \"legacy (a one-member milestone inherits its spec; others and roadmaps owe their own review)\", \"legacy (owes its own review)\"\n\t}\n\tmilestone, _ = docs.Review[MilestoneReviewRequiredKey].(string)\n\troadmap, _ = docs.Review[RoadmapReviewRequiredKey].(string)\n\treturn true, milestone, roadmap\n}\n\nfunc closeoutReviewPolicyCatalogEntry() CatalogEntry {\n\treturn CatalogEntry{\n\t\tID: \"closeout-review-policy\", Summary: \"milestone and roadmap reviews by cost and benefit\", IntroducedIn: \"7.4.1\", DefaultForNew: true,\n\t\tEffect: \"the close of a milestone or a roadmap owes its own review only as milestone_review_required and roadmap_review_required say (never, when-justified, always); `pose close` stays explicit and records why\",\n\t\tAdopt: func(docs PolicyDocs, _ string) []string {\n\t\t\tif closeoutPairPresent(docs) {\n\t\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tchanges, _ := SetCloseoutReviewPolicy(docs, CloseoutReviewNever, CloseoutReviewNever)\n\t\t\treturn changes\n\t\t},\n\t\tRetire:        func(PolicyDocs) []string { return nil },\n\t\tRetireRefusal: \"closeout-review-policy cannot be turned off: removing the pair would reinterpret closes already recorded under it; change the values with `pose adopt closeout-review-policy --milestone-review-required <v> --roadmap-review-required <v> --apply`\",\n\t\tAdopted:       func(docs PolicyDocs) bool { return closeoutPairPresent(docs) },\n\t}\n}\n75:func reviewAnswerAppliedIn(files posemodel.Files, root string, req reviewRequest) bool {\n96:func reviewAnswerApplied(root string, req reviewRequest) bool {\n435:func applyReviewAnswer(root string, req reviewRequest, date, issuer, givenReason string) (string, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/legacy_ledger.go:382:func PlanAdoptionEffects(root, capability, issuer string, now time.Time) ([]AdoptionEffect, error) {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
