{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: approved\n\nNo defects established. Focused and broader relevant tests passed; artifact and surface checks found no blocking issues. Both full validation reruns timed out at 600 seconds, so the validation conclusions below rely on the sealed passing evidence, not those reruns.\n\nApplied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation, and delivery-evidence rules. The worktree is unchanged; no attestation was recorded. The acknowledged coverage gap is that `adopt.values` was verified by code inspection rather than a direct test.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"prior_findings\": [],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed R1-R3, constraints and non-goals; all eight scoped paths in 43099880d96a55d195811bf1f5269a9a3d14073d..5f9eec2eb9d168c10217a289b144495c8866304e; request loading, already-applied handling, catalog adoption, policy loading/publication, adoption effects, direct-command compatibility, setup/configuration-review consumers, tests, validation-matrix registration, and all four manual copies. Examined relevant knowledge and prior-round metadata. Ran focused regression tests, broader adoption/configuration/closeout/distribution tests across internal/pose, internal/cli, internal/mcpserver and internal/scaffold, artifact-check, surface-check, both strict validation commands, and diff/status checks. No previous findings were listed. Full validation reruns timed out; sealed passing evidence is retained explicitly.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified that preview and apply use the same catalog adoption implementation and date input: adopt.go:127-139 and configuration_review.go:435 onward. Policy maps are freshly decoded and preview does not publish them. The focused regression passed. R2's explanatory branch has no direct automated test, as the spec acknowledges; its defaults and command were checked against the catalog and CLI parser. Full validation reruns timed out, so their success is not assumed. No new accepted risk is asserted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The added work mutates local decoded maps only. It introduces no goroutines, shared mutable state, cancellation ownership or lifecycle changes; publication remains in the existing apply path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/configuration-review-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The CLI adds the specified adopt.change and adopt.values output. Request identity, answers, pair-flag refusal, file schemas and MCP contracts remain unchanged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing request validation and pair-flag rejection remain active. The new policy-load failure returns a contextual failure and exit code 1; no new unbounded input processing is introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/configuration-review-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Checked configuration-review requests, setup consumers, catalog adoption and existing adoption effects. Broader relevant tests passed across domain, CLI, MCP-server and scaffold packages.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Preview now reports catalog changes through the established adopt.change field. Policy-load errors include actionable context; the added explanation contains no secret material.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/configuration-review-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared request and direct adoption paths. The change adds the output promised by the spec without altering stored policy formats, request authority, adopted values or public MCP interfaces.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The focused regression command passed independently. Broader selected tests also passed in all four affected supporting packages. Catalog change descriptions are produced before existing adoption-effect descriptions, and preview remains non-publishing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-096bd339669c7354\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1's cause was omission of catalog policy changes from the request preview. adopt.go:127-139 invokes the same catalog function used by apply on independently loaded maps, avoiding duplicate policy-setting logic. R2 adds the alternative-values command beside those changes. R3 corrects attribution in the distributed prose. No individual structural facts requiring mappings were listed in the brief.\",\n      \"mappings\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected all four manual diffs. English and Portuguese root/scaffold copies consistently attribute the qualified sandboxed Claude profile to pose-dist, preserving the surrounding operational instructions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The closeout catalog produces the explicit never/never changes, and adopt.values names the complete direct command and allowed values for choosing alternatives. Existing request and policy failures retain contextual errors.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1 is covered by the independently passing preview/apply regression and shared catalog implementation. R2 was verified against adopt.go:136-137, the closeout catalog defaults and CLI usage. R3 was verified in all four manual copies and distribution-related tests. The constraint refusing pair flags remains tested.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scoped implementation is a small preview-only addition, a regression test, validation registration and four attribution edits. Apply semantics and parametrized request answers remain outside this change, as required by the non-goals.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/configuration-review-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected the scoped diff and request-to-policy path. No new command execution, dependencies, credentials, path construction or authority changes were introduced. Preview changes only local decoded maps; existing request validation and guarded publication remain responsible for apply.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-096bd339669c7354\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing the catalog's existing adoption function is the smallest sufficient way to keep preview descriptions aligned with writes. A separate planner or duplicated key list would add unnecessary contracts. The change adds no speculative abstraction. This choice would need reconsideration if catalog adoption acquired external side effects or stopped returning complete change descriptions.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed the required command and inspected a filtered JSON rerun: 955 repository-wide warnings, no error or critical findings. Also examined the explicit sealed range.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-096bd339669c7354\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the sealed structural evidence and independently inspected the implementation and requirement basis. Did not run an assessment producer that could write repository artifacts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A component assessment refresh was unnecessary for this bounded review and could write under .pose. Inspected the mapped component directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/configuration-review-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Preserved the no-write boundary. Inspected catalog, CLI, configuration-review and setup integration directly; no REST, event or MCP contract changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Preserved the no-write boundary. Inspected the complete scoped code diff for debt markers and incomplete branches; no new TODO, FIXME, stub or panic was introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose context --task spec:pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion depends on POSE recording and verifying this review conclusion. The reviewer was explicitly instructed not to record an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose context --task spec:pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Cannot establish this review's completion before its conclusion is recorded and verified by POSE.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Resolved and read the review workflow and applicable Go, security and documentation rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets --strict: one target, 218 results, zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This disposition uses the sealed successful validation producer. Independently ran pose validate --strict; that rerun returned failure because pose-mcp's full unit check exceeded 600 seconds, with 217 checks passing and one timeout. The rerun is not claimed as passing and the timeout does not establish a defect in this scoped change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This disposition uses the sealed successful module validation evidence. Independently ran pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp; its full unit check likewise timed out at 600 seconds. The focused required regression and broader selected adoption/configuration/closeout/distribution tests passed independently.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
